# etc/rc with the kernel's key store holding keys (boot-arg aks_keys=1, iokit/Kernel/MiniAppleKeyStore.cpp; HakiOS's
# MediaTek branch's rc.launchd.aks): before launchd what its boot task "keybag" (keybagd --init) does on a device and
# skips when it boots from a RAM disk -- the system bag made once, as a restore would (src/aks_restore.c), then loaded.
# Bluetooth wants it: bluetoothd keeps its identity root and each paired device's keys in the keychain (6T, run 91: a
# paired keyboard gone when Settings looked again).
/redwood/bin/aks_restore
/usr/libexec/keybagd --init
exec /sbin/launchd.darwin
